{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PS4 fixes a CI flake this change itself introduced (not pre-existing on origin/main). The S2a import-isolation test did sys.modules.pop('pydantic_ai', 'rebar_reconciler', ...) without restoring, poisoning the shared pytest-xdist worker — surfacing intermittently as 'module pydantic_ai has no attribute models' in test_pai_output/test_llm_failure_classifier and split-module-identity failures in test_doctor_dirty_tree (run A red / run B green on the same PS3 commit). Rewrote the check to run in a fresh subprocess (no global sys.modules mutation) and narrowed the forbidden set to the honest shadow-phase guarantee. Teeth: injecting an eager 'import pydantic_ai' into _registry drives it RED."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787187840502179001,"uuid":"f1c07750-7234-4545-a4c5-fcf46c8ec7ed"}